      <workList xml:id="idm66">
         <work xml:id="work_d1e177174">
            <identifier label="SchW" xml:id="identifier_dd186139">A6:002</identifier>
            <title xml:id="title_154N20092" xml:lang="de">Eine große Serenate</title>
            <contributor xml:id="respStmt_bb1e21ea">
               <persName role="composer" xml:id="persName_154N20098">Johann Adolph Scheibe</persName>
            </contributor>
            <history xml:id="history_154N2009B">
               <p xml:id="idm74">The only reference to the present work is a newspaper advertisement in <rend xml:id="idm75" fontstyle="italic">Kiøbenhavns Adresse-Contoirs Efterretninger </rend>that appeared in 1780. The work, which included both score and orchestral material, was part of a lot including musical works by late eighteenth-century composers such as <persName xml:id="idm76" auth="VIAF" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" role="">Benda</persName>, <persName xml:id="idm77" auth="VIAF" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" role="">Zielche</persName>, <persName xml:id="idm78" auth="VIAF" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" role="">Graun</persName>, and <persName xml:id="idm79" auth="VIAF" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" role="">Pugnani</persName> as well as six works by Scheibe. There is no indication in the advertisement as to whom the seller was. As Scheibe in other instances describes cantatas as 'Serenaten', it is possible that the present work was a large cantata for orchestra and vocal soloists, and possibly also including a choir.</p>
            </history>
            <langUsage xml:id="langUsage_579262d6">
               <language xml:id="da">Danish</language>
               <language xml:id="de">German</language>
            </langUsage>
            <biblList xml:id="listBibl_cedccbc3-39ae-4bbf-931a-9d01dbd5c0b6221">
